        <div class="note" style="margin-top: 24px; max-width: 60ch;">
            <strong>iPhone 13 Pro, iPhone X, iPhone 6, iPhone 5s, AirPods Max 2,
            and every item originally under Accessories</strong> use images
            hotlinked from
            <a href="https://dummyjson.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DummyJSON</a>,
            a free placeholder REST API built for prototyping, not stored in this
            repository. Unlike the CC-licensed photos above, DummyJSON publishes no
            explicit image license, its images are almost certainly mirrored real
            product photography being used here the way the whole developer
            community uses this API: for prototyping, not as a rights-cleared
            asset. Swap these for licensed photography before any real deployment.
            AirPods Max 2 reuses the same photo already hotlinked for this
            catalog's original AirPods Max: the external shell design hasn't
            changed between the two generations.
        </div>

        <p style="max-width: 60ch; margin-top: 16px; font-size: 0.85rem;" class="empty-state">
            The newer product names (iPhone 17/Air, Watch Series 11/Ultra 3, and
            as of this catalog expansion Watch Series 12/Ultra 4 and AirPods 5)
            don't always have a photo of that exact model under a free license
            yet; where that's true, the closest real, correctly-identified prior
            generation was used and labeled as such in the table above, rather
            than an older or visibly mismatched photo passed off as current. The
            AirPods Pro 3 photo is a genuine current-generation unit, just an
            unusual dark colorway rather than the standard white. A longer list
            of 2026 products and accessories that were researched but left out
            entirely, because no clean-licensed photo of the correct item could
            be found, is documented in this branch's migration comments rather
            than repeated here.
        </p>
